    <string name="open_home_settings">Open Home settings</string>
    <string name="fire_tv_title">About Home on Fire TV</string>
    <string name="fire_tv_body">Amazon Fire OS keeps the Home button bound to the Amazon launcher. Vitrum cannot change that without root or risky system modifications, which it never does.\n\nWhat you can do:\n• Open Vitrum from your apps list or the Recent row.\n• Use the ADB command below to launch it instantly (advanced users).\n• Consider a dedicated remote shortcut if your Fire TV firmware supports one.</string>
    <string name="fire_tv_adb">ADB command (informational):</string>
    <string name="fire_tv_adb_command">adb shell am start -n com.vitrum.tv/.MainActivity</string>
    <string name="android_tv_title">Set Vitrum as your Home app</string>
    <string name="android_tv_body">On Android TV and Google TV, open Home settings and choose Vitrum. The system asks you to confirm the new Home app.\n\nIf your TV does not show this option, the manufacturer may lock the default launcher. Vitrum still works when launched from the apps list.</string>
    <string name="android_tv_open">Open Home settings</string>
